WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.880
What does it take to turn Cenobites against each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.480
other? Perhaps even Pinhead's loyal&nbsp;
Chatterer isn't immune to betrayal.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.160
The horrifying Cenobite known as Chatterer has&nbsp;
been a part of the "Hellraiser" franchise since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.400
the very beginning. Even though he was&nbsp;
not referred to by that name, the demon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.900
was featured in the novella that introduced the&nbsp;
Cenobites, "The Hellbound Heart." Author Clive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.920
Barker's description is very close to how the&nbsp;
character would appear in his own film adaptation:

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.720
"Its features were so heavily scarified — the&nbsp;
wounds nurtured until they ballooned — that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.320
its eyes were invisible, and its words&nbsp;
corrupted by the disfigurement of its mouth."

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.880
One major difference between the original fiction&nbsp;
and the film adaptation is that Chatterer could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:40.080
actually speak at first, though most likely he&nbsp;
was hard to understand. In the films and comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.620
the creature only communicates through the&nbsp;
rather disturbing trademark of clicking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.740
his exposed teeth together instead&nbsp;
of spewing out garbled sentences.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.240
In the first "Hellraiser" film and its sequel,&nbsp;
Chatterer was played by Nicholas Vince,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:55.800
who made his screen debut with the role. According&nbsp;
to Paul Kane, author of "The Hellraiser Films and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:00.420
Their Legacy," Vince was a drama student enrolled&nbsp;
at Mountview Theatre School in London when he met&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:05.040
Clive Barker. One of Vince's classmates was Simon&nbsp;
Bamford, who was a member of Barker's theater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.720
group, the Dog Company. Bamford would later accept&nbsp;
a role as one of the Cenobites, and it was through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:14.280
him that Vince met Barker at a party, which led to&nbsp;
a discussion about working together shortly after.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.720
In an interview with Devolution Magazine, Vince&nbsp;
briefly described his working relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.200
with Barker during the years leading up to&nbsp;
the production of the iconic horror flick:

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.520
"I ended up modeling for the covers of 'Books&nbsp;
of Blood' and I think I'm on four out of six,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:31.140
either my head or bits of my body. So, Clive&nbsp;
had known me for nearly three years by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.380
time 'Hellraiser' came about. He knew&nbsp;
I could do physical stuff so he said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.900
'Would you like to be in a movie?&nbsp;
There is some makeup involved.'"

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.600
As it turned out, that was&nbsp;
something of an understatement.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.520
"The box. You opened it. We came."

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.300
Almost nothing is known about Chatterer&nbsp;
until the second film, "Hellbound:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.200
Hellraiser 2," which features a brief glimpse&nbsp;
of what the creature looked like as a human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.460
before his horrific transformation. After&nbsp;
the film's evil doctor antagonist mutates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:00.720
into the powerful Channard Cenobite, he faces&nbsp;
off against Pinhead and his demon followers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.860
including Chatterer. Even though Channard&nbsp;
is outnumbered, he slays each foe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.520
which reveals their past forms. That's&nbsp;
when we see Chatterer as a young boy.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.900
When talking with Devolution Magazine, actor&nbsp;
Nicholas Vince admitted he was upset at first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:16.980
about the way that scene was captured on film.&nbsp;
But as he fleshed out his own backstory for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:20.880
the character, he became more intrigued by&nbsp;
the concept of a child Cenobite. He said,

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.900
"I realize I was really pissed off that the&nbsp;
moment Chatterer changes you didn't get to see me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:30.000
you got to see a boy. Over the years I found the&nbsp;
idea of a boy growing up in hell fascinating. All&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.478
the other Cenobites are revealed to be adults, but&nbsp;
a boy? That whole idea was really interesting."

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:39.300
Once Chatterer had become a member of Pinhead's&nbsp;
entourage, one of his early victims was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:43.380
celebrity Janice Baur. In the short story&nbsp;
"Losing Herself in the Part" from "Clive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:47.760
Barker's Hellraiser" #8, the actress rejects&nbsp;
a role offered by director Steven Sigourney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.480
because she cannot relate to the level of pain&nbsp;
her character has gone through. In response,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.620
Sigourney hands her the Lament Configuration&nbsp;
and asks her to carry out an acting exercise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.760
with it by getting the puzzle box into the&nbsp;
Shape of Pain. Intrigued by this new method,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.800
she takes the box home and works on it right away.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:06.900
Baur's fascination turns dark quickly as she&nbsp;
cuts her hands for days to solve the puzzle. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:11.520
also begins to have vivid nightmares of Hell. Her&nbsp;
descent into madness made her feel ready to accept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:16.440
the part, but that's when the Lament Configuration&nbsp;
opens and sends the actress into Hell. There,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:20.400
she is tortured by Chatterer and the other&nbsp;
Cenobites while Sigourney films it all. Baur&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.840
then continues to act in films, but her life is&nbsp;
dominated by the creatures of Hell from then on.

00:03:25.857 --> 00:03:30.660
In "Hellraiser Nightbreed: Jihad" #1 and #2,&nbsp;
the Cenobites initially confront the Nightbreed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:35.280
in an epic crossover showdown between two of&nbsp;
Clive Barker's most popular universes. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.600
before long it becomes clear that Alastor,&nbsp;
the Cenobite waging war on the Nightbreed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.680
intends to carry out a complete purge of&nbsp;
his foe, which defies Leviathan's will.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:48.420
In response, the God of Pain and Pleasure orders&nbsp;
Chatterer and Pinhead to destroy the heretic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:52.740
and his followers. When the demonic warriors&nbsp;
encounter Alastor and his Cenobite entourage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:57.240
he's quickly abandoned by all his followers&nbsp;
except for his lover Chalkis, who is bound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:01.380
to him with a golden chain. Once the couple is&nbsp;
defeated, Leviathan reverts them to their human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:05.417
bodies and the two are hunted down by one of the&nbsp;
Nightbreed that they had tried to exterminate.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:09.840
Pinhead has several followers in his demonic&nbsp;
crew throughout the "Hellraiser" series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:13.680
but Chatterer is often depicted as the&nbsp;
leader's top lieutenant among the Cenobites.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:17.460
He has appeared in more "Hellraiser" films&nbsp;
than any of the others, aside from Pinhead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:21.180
so the character has a prominent spot&nbsp;
within the nightmarish universe. Even so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.700
this didn't save him from the&nbsp;
cruel wrath of his leader.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:28.020
"Your suffering will be legendary. Even in hell."

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:32.940
While the first Chatterer was killed off in the&nbsp;
second film, he was resurrected 20 years later by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:37.860
Pinhead in the "Hellraiser" comic series. Pinhead&nbsp;
himself was revived once the Pillar of Souls was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:42.240
fed blood in "Hellraiser 3: Hell on Earth," so&nbsp;
their master used the same method to bring back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:46.320
Chatterer and the Female Cenobite with bloodshed&nbsp;
on the very spot where they had met their demise.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:49.320
Later, in the fifth chapter of&nbsp;
"Clive Barker's Hellraiser Omnibus",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:52.980
Pinhead and the Cenobites confront Kirsty&nbsp;
Cotton again and have her in their grasp.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:57.540
Yet instead of taking the heroine out, Pinhead&nbsp;
traps his own followers in his chains despite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:02.160
their pleas. He then hands Kirsty a knife and&nbsp;
she uses it to slay the Cenobite once more.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.540
Pinhead may have been directly responsible&nbsp;
for the second death of his servant in "Clive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:10.500
Barker's Hellraiser Omnibus," but another&nbsp;
tale shows how Chatterer finally achieved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:15.000
gruesome revenge for the betrayal. Over a decade&nbsp;
before Gary Tunnicliffe directed the tenth film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.140
"Hellraiser: Judgment," he released a&nbsp;
short fan flick in 2004 called "No More&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:21.960
Souls," which could be considered&nbsp;
official canon for the series.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:26.640
The story takes place in the distant future after&nbsp;
humanity has destroyed itself and Hell no longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:31.080
has any souls to reap. In desperation over the&nbsp;
depletion of such a valuable resource, Pinhead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:35.700
opens the Lament Configuration to sacrifice&nbsp;
himself. The Cenobites then emerge to slay their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:40.860
master, and Chatterer nails Pinhead's ripped-off&nbsp;
face to a Torture Pillar, signifying his true end.

